A real enterprise system rarely uses only one architecture.

For example:

```text
                         Clients
                            │
                            ↓
                      API Gateway
                            │
             ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
             ↓              ↓              ↓
          Ordering       Payment       Inventory
          Context        Context         Context
             │              │              │
             ↓              ↓              ↓
        Clean/Hexagonal Architectures
             │              │              │
             └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                            ↓
                       Event Broker
                            │
              ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
              ↓             ↓             ↓
          Analytics       Email          Audit
```

Possible architecture:

```text
DDD
 +
Microservices
 +
Clean Architecture
 +
Hexagonal Architecture
 +
Event-Driven Architecture
 +
CQRS
 +
Saga
 +
API Gateway
 +
BFF
```

Each solves a different problem.

