# 26. Architecture Selection Examples

## Small/Medium Business Application

A reasonable architecture:

```text
Modular Monolith
       +
Clean Architecture
       +
DDD
```

Don't introduce microservices without a clear requirement.

---

## Large Enterprise Platform

Possible architecture:

```text
Microservices
      +
DDD
      +
Event-Driven
      +
API Gateway
      +
Saga
      +
CQRS where justified
```

---

## Legacy Modernization

Use:

```text
Strangler Fig
      +
Modularization
      +
Incremental Migration
      +
Event-driven integration where appropriate
```

---

# 27. Architectural Trade-Offs

There is no universally "best" architecture.

Every decision involves trade-offs.

| Decision         | Benefit                        | Cost                        |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------------------- |
| Monolith         | Simplicity                     | Limited independent scaling |
| Microservices    | Independent scaling/deployment | Distributed complexity      |
| CQRS             | Optimized read/write models    | More complexity             |
| Event-driven     | Loose coupling                 | Eventual consistency        |
| Event Sourcing   | Complete history               | High complexity             |
| Saga             | Distributed workflow           | Compensation complexity     |
| Serverless       | Low infrastructure management  | Vendor/runtime constraints  |
| API Gateway      | Centralized entry point        | Additional infrastructure   |
| BFF              | Client optimization            | More backend components     |
| Modular Monolith | Strong boundaries + simplicity | Single deployment           |

