# 32. Golden Rule for Architects

> **Architecture is not about knowing more patterns. Architecture is about knowing when NOT to use them.**

The strongest architect can explain:

```text
WHY this architecture?
WHY NOT another architecture?
WHAT are the trade-offs?
WHAT happens when it fails?
HOW will it scale?
HOW will it evolve?
HOW will we operate it?
HOW much will it cost?
```

That is the difference between **knowing architecture** and **doing architecture**.
